1. d4 d5 2. c4 { The Queen's Gambit: the c-pawn challenges d5 to win central control. }
2... dxc4 3. Nf3 { [%name Classical, 3.Nf3] Stops ...e5 before regaining the pawn with e3 and Bxc4. }
( 3. e4 { [%name Central, 3.e4] Taking the whole centre at once. }
  3... Nf6
  ( 3... e5 { [%name Central, 3...e5] }
    4. Nf3 exd4 5. Bxc4 Nc6 6. O-O Be6 7. Bxe6 fxe6 8. Qb3 { Hitting the weakened e6 and b7. }
    8... Qd7 9. Qxb7 Rb8 10. Qa6 { White is a pawn up for now; Black has open lines for the rooks. } )
  4. e5 Nd5 5. Bxc4 Nb6 6. Bb3 Nc6 7. Ne2 { The knight supports d4 and keeps the f-pawn free. }
  7... Bf5 8. Nbc3 e6 9. O-O )
3... Nf6 4. e3 e6 5. Bxc4 { The pawn is back and White has the freer game. }
5... c5 6. O-O a6 7. a4 { Stopping ...b5, which would gain queenside space with tempo. }
7... Nc6 8. Qe2 cxd4 9. Rd1 Be7 10. exd4 O-O 11. Nc3 { White accepts an isolated d-pawn for active pieces and attacking chances. } *
